/Keywords (*ARTILLERY;*ARMY OPERATIONS;*LESSONS LEARNED;NIGHT WARFARE;SMOKE MUNITIONS;HELICOPTERS;LANDING FIELDS;MILITARY TACTICS;NIGHT FLIGHT;VIETNAM;TELESCOPES;ARTILLERY FIRE;AIRMOBILE OPERATIONS;COUNTERINSURGENCY;LANDING LIGHTS;HOWITZERS;ENEMY PERSONNEL;WHITE PHOSPHORUS;CLOSE SUPPORT;SOUTH VIETNAM;AERIAL RECONNAISSANCE;DEPLOYMENT)
/Subject (Operation JEB STUART III, which began on 17 May 68, continued throughout the reporting period. This operation was primarily geared toward destruction of the Viet Cong infrastructure and denial of rice to the enemy. Since 1 August 1968 the operation has been characterized by small unit contacts and seizure of several significant rice caches.)
/Title (Lessons Learned, Headquarters, 1st Cavalry Division Artillery \(Airmobile\))
